# Calibre reload (dev)

Always reinstall: `python makeplugin.py install` (no `--restart`) after repo changes, then tell the user to restart Calibre.

Do **not** quit/restart Calibre on every change. Restart only when this session must load the new zip in the GUI now (plugin UI iteration).

If you restart:

- Prefer **calibre-dev** MCP (`install_plugin`, `restart_calibre`, `calibre_status`) over shell `kill`/`open`.
- Or `python makeplugin.py install --restart --agent-id <short-name>`.
- One restart at a time. If the tool returns `error: locked`, skip — another agent owns it. Do not `killall calibre`.

```bash
python makeplugin.py install
python makeplugin.py install --restart --agent-id ui-pass
python makeplugin.py status
```
